I tried to get to a corner where my stash was - but accidentally
teleported it away when I tried to teleport the archons in my way.
Didn't find the stash till the end of the battle.

However, since that square was in an Elbereth-marked corner, Getting
there would mean that only the A's would attack me, and once I whittled
them down, I could deal with the Xorns.  This didn't exactly work,
since the A's wouldn't come to me, and everytime there was an empty
square, something new would be summoned there.  Cockatrice corpses
weren't that great either (though I was deathly afraid of something
wielding one of those against me), because xorns are petrification
resistant.  Instead, I had to hack my way to the archons myself.  I
used a whole bunch of charges from my wand of fire (charging it once,
and picking up a spare during the fighting) to carve paths of Elbereth
marked squares through the hordes of monsters, just to be able to reach
an A.

The good news was that because of all the extra monsters, I could rest
and heal up in between, since very few monsters were willing to attack
me while I was standing on an E-marked square, though I still kept on
getting dizzy from the occasional Umber Hulk.  If I hadn't wished for
the Eyes, things could have been much worse (Archon Radiance).

The monsters in my way never stopped coming, so I put on my ring of
conflict.  This finally made it easier to move around and target the
archons and ki-rin.  I started walking through the horde, targeting
them one at a time.  At one point a bunch of fire giants were created
and left boulders, and the only way I could get through them was
stone-to-flesh, which I was very reluctant to use at first, since this
would just re-animate all those beasts I whacked with the rubber
chicken.  In the end I didn't see any other option, and made a note to
kill A's the hard way.


